This licence is written in the shape of the PolyForm licences — short sections,
plain words, second person — because that shape is readable. It is not one of
them, it is not endorsed by them, and it says different things. Read it; it is
two pages.

## Acceptance

To get any licence under these terms you must agree to them, as both strict
obligations and conditions to everything they grant you.

## Copyright Licence

The licensor grants you a copyright licence to **use** the software for any
permitted purpose.

That licence covers everything you might do with the software that would
otherwise infringe the licensor's copyright in it, other than the things
[No Other Rights](#no-other-rights) keeps back — in particular making changes
and distributing the source.

## Permitted Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.

**Personal uses.** Use for personal study, research, experiment and testing,
private entertainment, hobby projects, amateur pursuits or religious
observance, without any anticipated commercial application, is use for a
permitted purpose.

**Noncommercial organisations.** Use by a charitable organisation, an
educational institution, a public research organisation, a public safety or
health organisation, an environmental protection organisation or a government
institution is use for a permitted purpose, whatever the source of its funding.

**Commercial use is not permitted** and needs a separate written agreement with
the licensor. Use by or for a company, in the course of its own work, is
commercial use — whatever the diagram is of, and whether or not anything is
sold. So is any use that ends up in something offered for sale.

## Running It For Others

Running the software so that other people can use it — a shared instance, an
internal service, the playground on a machine other people reach — is use like
any other, and is permitted as long as it is for a permitted purpose. Offering
it to anyone as a paid or commercial service is not.

## Passing On A Build

The licensor grants you a copyright licence to give another person a copy of a
**build**, provided that:

1. you pass it on exactly as you received it, unchanged;
2. you pass on a copy of these terms with it;
3. the person receiving it is within the permitted purposes above; and
4. you charge nothing, directly or indirectly, for doing so.

You get no licence to distribute the software in any other way.

## The Source Is Confidential

The source code is the licensor's confidential information, and this licence
grants you nothing in respect of it.

If you have been given access to the source, that access is **personal to
you**. You may not copy it, publish it, mirror it, pass it to anyone else, or
make it available to anyone else, in whole or in part, by any means.

## No Changes

You may not modify the software, or make anything based on it. A copy you have
altered is not a build, and [Passing On A Build](#passing-on-a-build) does not
cover it.

This does not stop you from writing your own software that reads or writes
files the software reads or writes.

## Patent Licence

The licensor grants you a patent licence for the software that covers patent
claims the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that you would
infringe by using the software as these terms permit.

## Patent Defence

If you make any written claim that the software infringes or contributes to
infringement of any patent, your patent licence for the software ends
immediately. If your company makes such a claim, your patent licence ends
immediately for work on behalf of your company.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not allow you to sublicense or transfer any of your licences to
anyone else, and do not prevent the licensor from granting licences to anyone
else. They do not imply any other licences.

## Fair Use

You may have "fair use", "fair dealing" or equivalent rights in the software
under the law. These terms do not limit them.

## Violations

The first time you are notified in writing that you have violated any of these
terms, or done anything with the software that your licences do not cover, your
licences can nonetheless continue if you come into full compliance and take
practical steps to correct past violations within 32 days of receiving notice.
Otherwise all your licences end immediately.

## No Liability

***As far as the law allows, the software comes as is, without any warranty or
condition, and the licensor will not be liable to you for any damages arising
out of these terms or the use or nature of the software, under any kind of
legal claim.***

## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these terms, and the
**software** is the software the licensor makes available under them.

**You** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these terms.

**Your company** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship or other kind of
organisation that you work for, plus all organisations that have control over,
are under the control of, or are under common control with that organisation.
**Control** means ownership of substantially all the assets of an entity, or
the power to direct its management and policies by vote, contract or otherwise.
Control can be direct or indirect.

A **build** is a compiled or packaged copy of the software published by the
licensor — a binary, an editor extension, a package, an archive from the
licensor's releases — that you have not altered.

The **source code** is the human-readable form of the software, including the
contents of the licensor's repository.

**Your licences** are all the licences granted to you for the software under
these terms.

**Use** means anything you do with the software requiring one of your licences.
